.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-veil-cat 1  "git-veil-cat " 
.SH NAME
git\-veil\-cat \- Decrypt a single tracked file to stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-veil cat\fR [\fB\-\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-store\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decrypt a single tracked file to stdout
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Your email address
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Git remote name
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-store\fR \fI<KEY_STORE>\fR
Key store directory (default: $GIT_VEIL_HOME or $HOME/.git\-veil)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
File to decrypt
.SH EXTRA
Decrypts a single tracked file to stdout without touching disk state:
neither the plaintext nor its .secret ciphertext is modified. The keyring
signature is verified against the pinned trusted key first, and the file
must be tracked with its ciphertext present beside it.

EXAMPLES
  $ git\-veil cat .env
  $ git\-veil cat .env \-\-email alice@example.com
